+# z/OS CCSID Conversion Test Suite
+
+## Overview
+Comprehensive test suite for validating z/OS CCSID conversion fixes for critical issues #2, #4, and #5 from the AI review.
+
+## Test Files
+
+### 1. zos-ccsid-conversion_test.py
+**Purpose:** Core functionality tests for CCSID conversion
+
+**Tests:**
+- **Test 1:** Multibyte UTF-8 characters across block boundaries (Issue #2)
+  - Tests various block sizes (16, 64, 512, 8192 bytes)
+  - Verifies multibyte sequences (Spanish, Japanese, Chinese, Greek) are preserved
+  - Ensures no EINVAL errors or mixed-encoding corruption
+
+- **Test 2:** Large files (>64KB) with multibyte content
+  - 10,000 lines with UTF-8 characters
+  - Tests stateful conversion across multiple 64KB chunks
+  - Verifies complete file integrity
+
+- **Test 3:** Delta transfers with matched blocks (Issue #5)
+  - Initial EBCDIC file on z/OS
+  - Modify with UTF-8 characters from Linux
+  - Verify both matched and literal blocks converted correctly
+
+- **Test 4:** Invalid UTF-8 sequence handling (Issue #4)
+  - File with illegal byte sequences
+  - Verifies transfer FAILS (not silent corruption)
+  - Ensures no wrongly-tagged files created
+
+- **Test 5:** IBM-1047 newline handling
+  - Tests 0x25 (EBCDIC LF) → 0x15 (z/OS NL) conversion
+  - Verifies files readable by z/OS tools
+
+- **Test 6:** Edge cases (empty files, ASCII-only)
+  - Empty file handling
+  - ASCII-only files with minimal overhead
+
+- **Test 7:** Complex delta patterns
+  - 1000 lines with 1% modification
+  - Tests conversion with high match ratio
+
+- **Test 8:** Non-ASCII filenames
+  - UTF-8 characters in filenames
+  - Graceful handling if not supported
+
+**Run time:** ~5-10 minutes  
+**Prerequisites:** z/OS system with chtag, iconv, UTF-8 support
+
+---
+
+### 2. zos-ccsid-performance_test.py
+**Purpose:** Performance benchmarking and overhead measurement
+
+**Tests:**
+- **Test 1:** Conversion overhead comparison
+  - 10MB ASCII-only file (no conversion)
+  - 10MB mixed ASCII/UTF-8 file (with conversion)
+  - Calculates overhead percentage
+  - **Acceptance:** <20% overhead (warning at >50%)
+
+- **Test 2:** Large file throughput
+  - 100MB file with UTF-8 content
+  - Measures end-to-end time and MB/s throughput
+  - **Acceptance:** >10MB/s on local disk
+
+- **Test 3:** Delta transfer efficiency
+  - 50MB base file
+  - Modify 1% of content
+  - Measure speedup vs full transfer
+  - **Acceptance:** >2x speedup for 1% changes
+
+- **Test 4:** Block size impact
+  - Test block sizes: 512, 2048, 8192, 32768
+  - Identifies optimal block size
+  - Reports throughput for each
+
+**Run time:** ~15-30 minutes  
+**Prerequisites:** z/OS system with sufficient disk space (>500MB)
+
+---
+
+### 3. zos-ccsid-regression_test.py
+**Purpose:** Ensure existing functionality not broken by changes
+
+**Tests:**
+- **Test 1:** Basic transfer without --zos-tags
+- **Test 2:** Transfer with --no-zos-tags
+- **Test 3:** ASCII/UTF-8 files bypass conversion
+- **Test 4:** Binary files
+- **Test 5:** Directories and symlinks
+- **Test 6:** --inplace option
+- **Test 7:** --append option
+- **Test 8:** --checksum option
+- **Test 9:** --whole-file option
+- **Test 10:** Compression (-z)
+- **Test 11:** --delete option
+- **Test 12:** Dry run (-n)
+- **Test 13:** Sparse files
+
+**Run time:** ~5-10 minutes  
+**Prerequisites:** z/OS system with full rsync feature set
+
